This project is an internal HR Copilot for the fictional company BluePeak Creative Group.
It uses:

• Next.js frontend
• Node.js backend
• RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) powered by OpenAI embeddings
• Your own HR documents (markdown files)

With it, you can ask internal questions like:

“How many PTO days do employees receive?”
“What is the probation period?”
“What does the NDA say about confidential info?”
“What documents are required for onboarding?”

1. Requirements

Make sure you have:

• Node.js 18+ installed
• npm installed
• OpenAI API key

2. Set up Backend

Move into backend folder:
cd backend

Install required packages:
npm install

Create .env file (inside backend folder):
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here

Make sure your HR documents are inside:
backend/data/
Allowed formats: .md or .txt.

Example files:

EmployeeHandbook.md
EmploymentContract.md
Hr_POLICIES_and_PROCEDURES_MANUAL.md
NDA.md
JOB_DESCRIPTIONS.md
ONBOARDING_CHECKLIST.md
ORGANIZATIONAL_CHART.md
ExitChecklist.md

Start backend:
node server.js

If everything is correct, you will see:

📄 Loading documents…
🧩 Total chunks: …
🧠 Computing embeddings…
✅ In-memory vector index ready.
🚀 Backend running on [http://localhost:3001](http://localhost:3001)

4. Set up Frontend (Next.js)

Move into frontend folder:
cd ../frontend

Install dependencies:
npm install

Run frontend dev server:
npm run dev

Open in browser:
[http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)
You will see a chat UI.

5. How to Use

Ask questions like:

“How many PTO days do employees receive?”
“What is the probation period?”
“What does the NDA say about confidential information?”
“What should a new employee do on their first day?”

The assistant will:

• search your documents using embeddings
• pick the most relevant chunks
• answer strictly from the document content
• show exactly which files were used

If the answer does NOT exist in the documents, you’ll see:

“Information not found in company documents.”

This prevents hallucinations.

6. Testing the Backend (optional)

You can test the backend separately with PowerShell:

Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "[http://localhost:3001/ask](http://localhost:3001/ask)" -Method Post -ContentType "application/json" -Body '{"question":"What is the probation period?"}'

7. Troubleshooting

Backend shows “Cannot find OpenAI key” → Check .env file: OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-…
“Information not found” → The document does not contain the answer. Add it and restart backend.
“Fetch failed” in frontend → Backend must be running on [http://localhost:3001](http://localhost:3001)

8. Summary

Once both servers are running:

Backend: [http://localhost:3001](http://localhost:3001)
Frontend: [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)

You now have a fully working RAG HR Assistant with document search, embeddings, GPT responses, and full hallucination protection.

